is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc0,r1,r11,r12,pc12
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: host OS kernel memory management on all path nodes (endpoints and routers). The network stack and routing daemons are healthy; the hiccups are caused by a periodic system task dropping kernel caches.

Mechanism: every ~2 minutes the nodes execute a cache purge (writing to /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches). That operation forces the kernel to reclaim page cache/dentries/inodes, briefly spiking CPU and stalling packet processing and userland I/O. During those short windows, TCP data paths “freeze” then recover once the system resumes normal scheduling, which matches the user’s symptoms.

Localization: evidence is present on all devices involved in the PC0↔PC12 path:
- pc0, r1, r11, r12, and pc1
